# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This section imports the tools and defines the shell-model helpers the workflow needs, in the order\n"
"the workflow uses them. The physics behind each one is derived in the [Appendix](#appendix); the\n"
"comments describe each function’s role in the workflow.\n"
msgstr "Ini-import ng seksyong ito ang mga tool at dine-define ang mga shell-model helper na kailangan ng workflow, ayon sa pagkakasunod-sunod ng paggamit ng workflow. Ang physics sa likod ng bawat isa ay hinango sa [Appendix](#appendix); inilalarawan ng mga comment ang papel ng bawat function sa workflow.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Two interaction files are unpacked first. Both are published parameter sets, embedded here so the\n"
"notebook is self-contained: `usda.snt` is the USDA $sd$-shell Hamiltonian [\\[2\\]](#references) and\n"
"`gxpf1.snt` is the GXPF1 $pf$-shell Hamiltonian [\\[3\\]](#references).\n"
msgstr "Unang ina-unpack ang dalawang interaction file. Parehong published na parameter set ang mga ito, naka-embed dito para self-contained ang notebook: ang `usda.snt` ay ang USDA $sd$-shell Hamiltonian [\\[2\\]](#references) at ang `gxpf1.snt` ay ang GXPF1 $pf$-shell Hamiltonian [\\[3\\]](#references).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The model space and the qubit register {#the-model-space-and-the-qubit-register}"
msgstr "Ang model space at ang qubit register {#the-model-space-and-the-qubit-register}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"An `.snt` file holds the model space, the single-particle energies, and the $J$-coupled two-body\n"
"matrix elements. For the mass-dependent interactions used here, the third and fourth fields of the two-body\n"
"header specify the reference mass\n"
"$A_{\\mathrm{ref}}$ at which the interaction was fitted and the exponent of its mass dependence. Both\n"
"files carry the exponent $-0.3$, with $A_{\\mathrm{ref}} = 18$ for USDA and $42$ for GXPF1, so the\n"
"tabulated matrix elements must be rescaled by $(A/A_{\\mathrm{ref}})^{-0.3}$ for the nucleus being\n"
"computed [\\[2\\]](#references), [\\[3\\]](#references). Single-particle energies are not rescaled. Skipping\n"
"this step changes the correlation energy by a few percent.\n"
msgstr "Ang isang `.snt` file ay naglalaman ng model space, ng mga single-particle energy, at ng mga $J$-coupled na two-body matrix element. Para sa mga mass-dependent na interaction na ginagamit dito, tinutukoy ng ikatlo at ikaapat na field ng two-body header ang reference mass na $A_{\\mathrm{ref}}$ kung saan na-fit ang interaction at ang exponent ng mass dependence nito. Parehong may exponent na $-0.3$ ang dalawang file, na may $A_{\\mathrm{ref}} = 18$ para sa USDA at $42$ para sa GXPF1, kaya ang mga naka-tabulate na matrix element ay dapat i-rescale ng $(A/A_{\\mathrm{ref}})^{-0.3}$ para sa nucleus na kino-compute [\\[2\\]](#references), [\\[3\\]](#references). Hindi nire-rescale ang mga single-particle energy. Kapag nilaktawan ang hakbang na ito, nagbabago ng ilang porsyento ang correlation energy.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The energies that follow are *valence* energies, measured from the inert core; they are not experimental\n"
"separation energies.\n"
msgstr "Ang mga energy na susunod ay mga *valence* energy, na sinusukat mula sa inert na core; hindi ang mga ito ang experimental separation energy.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Clebsch-Gordan recoupling {#clebsch-gordan-recoupling}"
msgstr "Clebsch-Gordan recoupling {#clebsch-gordan-recoupling}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Equation (2) requires Clebsch-Gordan coefficients for half-integer angular momenta. Every argument is\n"
"passed as *twice* its physical value, so $j = 5/2$ enters as `5` and the arithmetic stays exact.\n"
msgstr "Nangangailangan ang Equation (2) ng mga Clebsch-Gordan coefficient para sa mga half-integer na angular momentum. Ang bawat argumento ay ipinapasa bilang *dalawang beses* ng pisikal nitong halaga, kaya ang $j = 5/2$ ay pumapasok bilang `5` at nananatiling eksakto ang aritmetika.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`Interaction.v_ms` handles lookups of the interaction matrix elements. An `.snt` file stores each\n"
"matrix element once, so a lookup might need the antisymmetrized pair-exchange phase $-(-1)^{j_a + j_b - J}$ on either\n"
"side, and the bra and ket might be stored in either order.\n"
msgstr "Hinahawakan ng `Interaction.v_ms` ang mga lookup ng mga interaction matrix element. Isang beses lang iniimbak ng `.snt` file ang bawat matrix element, kaya maaaring kailanganin ng lookup ang antisymmetrized na pair-exchange phase na $-(-1)^{j_a + j_b - J}$ sa alinmang panig, at maaaring nakaimbak sa alinmang ayos ang bra at ket.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Matrix elements and the symmetry test {#matrix-elements-and-the-symmetry-test}"
msgstr "Mga matrix element at ang symmetry test {#matrix-elements-and-the-symmetry-test}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A determinant is a sorted tuple of occupied qubit indices. Two determinants differing in more than\n"
"two occupied states have a vanishing matrix element; otherwise, the Slater-Condon rules give a short\n"
"sum over the interaction, multiplied by a fermionic sign counting how many occupied states lie between the\n"
"operators in the fixed register ordering.\n"
msgstr "Ang determinant ay isang sorted na tuple ng mga occupied na qubit index. Ang dalawang determinant na magkaiba sa higit sa dalawang occupied state ay may naglalahong matrix element; kung hindi, ang mga Slater-Condon rule ay nagbibigay ng maikling sum sa interaction, na pinarami ng isang fermionic sign na bumibilang kung ilang occupied state ang nasa pagitan ng mga operator sa fixed na ayos ng register.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`symmetry_allowed` is the integer test that all four exact quantum numbers reduce to. It is used both\n"
"to filter samples and to enumerate the exact basis for the runs small enough to check.\n"
msgstr "Ang `symmetry_allowed` ang integer test na pinagbabawasan ng lahat ng apat na eksaktong quantum number. Ginagamit ito pareho sa pag-filter ng mga sample at sa pag-enumerate ng eksaktong basis para sa mga run na sapat na maliit para tsekin.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The reference determinant {#the-reference-determinant}"
msgstr "Ang reference determinant {#the-reference-determinant}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The ansatz is built on top of a single determinant, so that determinant should be the best one\n"
"available. Filling the lowest single-particle energies ignores the two-body interaction. In these model\n"
"spaces, that choice gives an energy 1–2 MeV above the lowest-energy determinant.\n"
msgstr "Ang ansatz ay binubuo sa ibabaw ng isang determinant, kaya dapat ang determinant na iyon ang pinakamahusay na magagamit. Ang pagpuno sa pinakamababang single-particle energy ay hindi pinapansin ang two-body interaction. Sa mga model space na ito, ang pagpiling iyon ay nagbibigay ng energy na 1–2 MeV sa itaas ng determinant na may pinakamababang energy.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Restricting to fillings made of time-reversed $(+m_j, -m_j)$ pairs forces $M_J = 0$ exactly and\n"
"leaves only $\\binom{n_{\\mathrm{pairs}}}{k}$ candidates per species (a few thousand at most), so the\n"
"best one can be found by searching them all on the full diagonal $\\langle \\Phi | H | \\Phi \\rangle$.\n"
"Ties go to the most strongly aligned pairs, where the $J = 0$ pairing force is strongest. In every\n"
"case in this tutorial that can be checked against a full enumeration, the search returns the global\n"
"lowest-diagonal determinant, which is also the largest single component of the exact ground state.\n"
msgstr "Ang paglilimita sa mga filling na binubuo ng time-reversed na $(+m_j, -m_j)$ pair ay pumipilit sa $M_J = 0$ nang eksakto at nag-iiwan lamang ng $\\binom{n_{\\mathrm{pairs}}}{k}$ na kandidato bawat species (ilang libo sa pinakamarami), kaya mahahanap ang pinakamahusay sa pamamagitan ng paghahanap sa lahat ng ito sa buong diagonal na $\\langle \\Phi | H | \\Phi \\rangle$. Ang mga tabla ay napupunta sa mga pair na pinakamalakas ang alignment, kung saan pinakamalakas ang $J = 0$ pairing force. Sa bawat kaso sa tutorial na ito na maaaring i-check laban sa buong enumeration, ibinabalik ng paghahanap ang global na lowest-diagonal determinant, na siya ring pinakamalaking single component ng exact ground state.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The excitation pool and its perturbative ranking {#the-excitation-pool-and-its-perturbative-ranking}"
msgstr "Ang excitation pool at ang perturbative ranking nito {#the-excitation-pool-and-its-perturbative-ranking}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Correlation is carried by two-particle–two-hole ($2p2h$) excitations from the reference. Two\n"
"selection rules reduce the pool before any circuit is built: an excitation must conserve $M_J$, and the hole pair and particle\n"
"pair must be able to couple to a common total $J$, which is a triangle inequality.\n"
msgstr "Ang correlation ay dala ng two-particle–two-hole ($2p2h$) na mga excitation mula sa reference. Dalawang selection rule ang nagpapaliit sa pool bago bumuo ng anumang circuit: ang excitation ay dapat mag-conserve ng $M_J$, at ang hole pair at particle pair ay dapat makapag-couple sa isang karaniwang kabuuang $J$, na isang triangle inequality.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The remaining excitations are ranked by the Epstein-Nesbet second-order score of selected configuration interaction\n"
"[\\[4\\]](#references),\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang natitirang mga excitation ay niraranggo ayon sa Epstein-Nesbet second-order score ng selected configuration interaction\n"
"[\\[4\\]](#references),\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation}\n"
"\\tag{3}\n"
"s_\\alpha = \\frac{|\\langle \\Phi_{\\mathrm{ref}} | H | \\alpha \\rangle|^2}{|\\Delta_\\alpha|},\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\Delta_\\alpha = H_{\\mathrm{ref},\\mathrm{ref}} - H_{\\alpha\\alpha},\n"
"\\end{equation}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation}\n"
"\\tag{3}\n"
"s_\\alpha = \\frac{|\\langle \\Phi_{\\mathrm{ref}} | H | \\alpha \\rangle|^2}{|\\Delta_\\alpha|},\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\Delta_\\alpha = H_{\\mathrm{ref},\\mathrm{ref}} - H_{\\alpha\\alpha},\n"
"\\end{equation}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"which estimates how much correlation energy each excitation carries. The same two numbers fix the\n"
"circuit angle: with $V = \\langle \\Phi_{\\mathrm{ref}} | H | \\alpha \\rangle$, the first-order amplitude\n"
"is $t_\\alpha = V / \\Delta_\\alpha$. The [Appendix](#appendix) explains why the first-order amplitude is\n"
"the choice used in this tutorial rather than the exact two-level angle.\n"
msgstr "na tumatantiya kung gaano karaming correlation energy ang dala ng bawat excitation. Ang parehong dalawang numero ang nagtatakda ng circuit angle: sa $V = \\langle \\Phi_{\\mathrm{ref}} | H | \\alpha \\rangle$, ang first-order amplitude ay $t_\\alpha = V / \\Delta_\\alpha$. Ipinaliliwanag ng [Appendix](#appendix) kung bakit ang first-order amplitude ang pinili sa tutorial na ito sa halip na ang eksaktong two-level angle.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Qubit-excitation blocks {#qubit-excitation-blocks}"
msgstr "Mga qubit-excitation block {#qubit-excitation-blocks}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Under the Jordan-Wigner mapping a particle-conserving $2p2h$ excitation operator becomes a sum of\n"
"eight Pauli strings, each carrying a string of $Z$ operators between the outermost indices. The\n"
"$Z$ strings enforce fermionic antisymmetry, and they are expensive: a proton-neutron\n"
"excitation spans the boundary between the two halves of the register and includes a parity string\n"
"across that boundary.\n"
msgstr "Sa ilalim ng Jordan-Wigner mapping, ang isang particle-conserving na $2p2h$ excitation operator ay nagiging sum ng walong Pauli string, na bawat isa ay may dalang string ng mga $Z$ operator sa pagitan ng pinakalabas na mga index. Ipinapatupad ng mga $Z$ string ang fermionic antisymmetry, at magastos ang mga ito: ang proton-neutron excitation ay sumasaklaw sa hangganan ng dalawang kalahati ng register at may kasamang parity string sa kabila ng hangganang iyon.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Dropping the $Z$ strings gives the *qubit-excitation* operator of Yordanov et al.\n"
"[\\[5\\]](#references). The state prepared by this operator has different amplitudes, but it connects exactly the same pairs of determinants, so the set of determinants the circuit can\n"
"reach is unchanged. Pooled SQD uses these determinants for the classical diagonalization. Step 2 compares\n"
"the support of the two constructions and measures their hardware costs.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang pag-alis ng mga $Z$ string ay nagbibigay ng *qubit-excitation* operator nina Yordanov et al.\n"
"[\\[5\\]](#references). Ang state na inihahanda ng operator na ito ay may magkaibang amplitude, ngunit nag-uugnay ito sa eksaktong parehong mga pares ng determinant, kaya hindi nagbabago ang set ng mga determinant na maaabot ng circuit. Ginagamit ng pooled SQD ang mga determinant na ito para sa classical diagonalization. Inihahambing ng Step 2 ang support ng dalawang construction at sinusukat ang mga hardware cost ng mga ito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Building the Pauli form from $a_j^\\dagger = \\tfrac{1}{2}(X_j - i Y_j) \\otimes Z_{<j}$, with the $Z$\n"
"string optional, keeps the two constructions a single flag apart. All eight terms of one generator\n"
"commute, so a single `PauliEvolutionGate` step is the exact exponential rather than a Trotter\n"
"approximation to it.\n"
msgstr "Ang pagbuo ng Pauli form mula sa $a_j^\\dagger = \\tfrac{1}{2}(X_j - i Y_j) \\otimes Z_{<j}$, na may opsyonal na $Z$ string, ay nagpapanatili sa dalawang construction na isang flag lang ang pagitan. Nagko-commute ang lahat ng walong term ng isang generator, kaya ang isang `PauliEvolutionGate` step ay ang eksaktong exponential at hindi isang Trotter approximation nito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The depth budget and the circuit ensemble {#the-depth-budget-and-the-circuit-ensemble}"
msgstr "Ang depth budget at ang circuit ensemble {#the-depth-budget-and-the-circuit-ensemble}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A single deep circuit containing every ranked excitation can exceed the hardware’s coherence time. Spreading the pool\n"
"over an *ensemble* of shallow circuits and pooling their shots into one determinant set turns Step 2\n"
"into a packing problem: each excitation has a measured cost, each circuit has a budget, and the\n"
"question is how much of the ranked pool fits.\n"
msgstr "Ang isang malalim na circuit na naglalaman ng bawat niraranggong excitation ay maaaring lumampas sa coherence time ng hardware. Ang pagkalat ng pool sa isang *ensemble* ng mga mababaw na circuit at pag-pool ng mga shot ng mga ito sa iisang determinant set ay ginagawang packing problem ang Step 2: bawat excitation ay may nasukat na cost, bawat circuit ay may budget, at ang tanong ay kung gaano karami sa niraranggong pool ang kasya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The budget is measured in **two-qubit depth** (layers of two-qubit gates on the critical path)\n"
"rather than in a raw gate count, because depth sets the circuit's duration and therefore how\n"
"much of the device's coherence it spends. The total count is reported alongside it, since that is the\n"
"better proxy for accumulated gate error; the two answer different questions and neither substitutes\n"
"for the other.\n"
msgstr "Ang budget ay sinusukat sa **two-qubit depth** (mga layer ng two-qubit gate sa critical path) sa halip na sa raw na bilang ng gate, dahil ang depth ang nagtatakda ng tagal ng circuit at kung gaano karami sa coherence ng device ang magagastos nito. Ang kabuuang bilang ay ini-report kasama nito, dahil iyon ang mas mahusay na proxy para sa naipong gate error; magkaiba ang sinasagot ng dalawa at hindi napapalitan ng isa ang isa pa.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Both quantities are extracted by *arity*: an instruction acting on exactly two qubits, whatever the\n"
"backend happens to call its entangling gate. Matching on gate names instead could return zero\n"
"for an unfamiliar basis set, incorrectly placing the whole pool in one circuit without exceeding\n"
"the computed budget.\n"
msgstr "Parehong dami ay kinukuha ayon sa *arity*: isang instruction na kumikilos sa eksaktong dalawang qubit, anuman ang itawag ng backend sa entangling gate nito. Ang pag-match sa mga pangalan ng gate ay maaaring magbalik ng zero para sa hindi pamilyar na basis set, na maling inilalagay ang buong pool sa isang circuit nang hindi lumalampas sa kinomputang budget.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Filling whichever circuit is currently emptiest, in rank order, keeps every circuit near the budget.\n"
"Costs are measured on the real backend target, one excitation at a time, because a cost read off an\n"
"abstract circuit is not the cost the transpiler produces.\n"
msgstr "Ang pagpuno sa alinmang circuit na pinakawalang laman sa kasalukuyan, ayon sa rank, ay nagpapanatili sa bawat circuit na malapit sa budget. Sinusukat ang mga cost sa totoong backend target, isang excitation bawat pagkakataon, dahil ang cost na binasa mula sa isang abstract na circuit ay hindi ang cost na nililikha ng transpiler.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Post-processing: repair, recombine, diagonalize {#post-processing-repair-recombine-diagonalize}"
msgstr "Post-processing: ayusin, pagsamahin muli, at i-diagonalize {#post-processing-repair-recombine-diagonalize}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Three helpers do the work of Step 4.\n"
msgstr "Tatlong helper ang gumagawa ng Step 4.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`half_configurations` splits each sampled row into a proton half and a neutron half, and keeps each\n"
"half that has the correct nucleon number. A row with a valid proton half contributes that half even if its\n"
"neutron half has the wrong nucleon number. Each half carries the total sampled weight of the rows it appeared in, which\n"
"is what ranks it if the subspace needs to be truncated.\n"
msgstr "Hinahati ng `half_configurations` ang bawat na-sample na row sa proton half at neutron half, at pinapanatili ang bawat half na may tamang nucleon number. Ang row na may valid na proton half ay nag-aambag ng half na iyon kahit mali ang nucleon number ng neutron half nito. Dala ng bawat half ang kabuuang sampled weight ng mga row kung saan ito lumitaw, na siyang nagra-rank dito kung kailangang i-truncate ang subspace.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`grow_subspace` recombines the halves into every product that lands in the target $M_J$ and parity\n"
"sector, *adding* to the subspace it is given rather than rebuilding it. That keeps successive\n"
"subspaces nested, which is what makes the energy sequence monotone non-increasing instead of merely\n"
"fluctuating around a bound.\n"
msgstr "Pinagsasama muli ng `grow_subspace` ang mga half sa bawat product na napupunta sa target na $M_J$ at parity sector, *dinadagdagan* ang subspace na ibinigay dito sa halip na buuin itong muli. Pinananatili nitong nested ang magkakasunod na subspace, kaya ang energy sequence ay monotone non-increasing sa halip na basta nagbabago-bago sa paligid ng isang bound.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`recovery_loop` is the self-consistent configuration recovery of the pooled SQD paper\n"
"[\\[1\\]](#references): repair the two half-register nucleon numbers against the current occupancy\n"
"estimate, recombine, diagonalize, and take the next occupancy estimate from the eigenvector.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang `recovery_loop` ay ang self-consistent configuration recovery ng pooled SQD paper\n"
"[\\[1\\]](#references): ayusin ang dalawang half-register na nucleon number laban sa kasalukuyang occupancy estimate, pagsamahin muli, i-diagonalize, at kunin ang susunod na occupancy estimate mula sa eigenvector.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Check the bit-ordering conventions carefully to avoid incorrect results. `qiskit-addon-sqd` writes column 0 of its\n"
"bitstring matrix as the *highest* qubit index, so reversing a row gives occupation indexed by qubit;\n"
"its \"right\" half is the low qubit indices, which is the proton block. Correspondingly,\n"
"`recover_configurations` takes `num_elec_a` as the proton number and average occupancies ordered\n"
"`(protons, neutrons)` by qubit index. The addon assumes bit $i$ pairs with bit $i + N$; in this\n"
"register, proton qubit $i$ and neutron qubit $i + N$ are the same $(n, \\ell, j, m_j)$ state, so the\n"
"assumption is physically meaningful here rather than incidental.\n"
msgstr "Maingat na tsekin ang mga bit-ordering convention para maiwasan ang maling resulta. Isinusulat ng `qiskit-addon-sqd` ang column 0 ng bitstring matrix nito bilang *pinakamataas* na qubit index, kaya ang pag-reverse ng isang row ay nagbibigay ng occupation na naka-index ayon sa qubit; ang \"kanang\" half nito ay ang mababang qubit index, na siyang proton block. Kaugnay nito, kinukuha ng `recover_configurations` ang `num_elec_a` bilang proton number at ang mga average na occupancy na nakaayos na `(protons, neutrons)` ayon sa qubit index. Ipinapalagay ng addon na ang bit $i$ ay ipinapares sa bit $i + N$; sa register na ito, ang proton qubit $i$ at neutron qubit $i + N$ ay iisang $(n, \\ell, j, m_j)$ state, kaya ang palagay ay may pisikal na kahulugan dito at hindi nagkataon lamang.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Backend, budget, and run parameters {#backend-budget-and-run-parameters}"
msgstr "Backend, budget, at mga run parameter {#backend-budget-and-run-parameters}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Every run that follows uses the same backend, the same pass managers, and the same depth budget, so the three\n"
"are directly comparable. The budget ties them together: every circuit in every\n"
"ensemble has to fit inside it, and it decides how much of a pool can be sampled at all.\n"
msgstr "Ang bawat run na susunod ay gumagamit ng parehong backend, parehong pass manager, at parehong depth budget, kaya direktang maihahambing ang tatlo. Pinag-uugnay sila ng budget: bawat circuit sa bawat ensemble ay dapat magkasya rito, at ito ang nagpapasya kung gaano karami sa isang pool ang maaaring ma-sample.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The values here were chosen by measuring transpiled cost against a Heron target. At a two-qubit depth of 300 and 16 circuits, both 24-qubit and 40-qubit ensembles come out well under 100 microseconds per\n"
"circuit, against coherence times of a few hundred microseconds. Increasing the budget includes more of the pool but increases circuit duration. Measure this\n"
"tradeoff for your backend.\n"
msgstr "Ang mga value dito ay pinili sa pamamagitan ng pagsukat ng transpiled na cost laban sa isang Heron target. Sa two-qubit depth na 300 at 16 na circuit, ang parehong 24-qubit at 40-qubit na ensemble ay lumalabas na mas mababa sa 100 microsecond bawat circuit, kumpara sa mga coherence time na ilang daang microsecond. Ang pagtaas ng budget ay nagsasama ng mas maraming bahagi ng pool ngunit pinahahaba ang tagal ng circuit. Sukatin ang tradeoff na ito para sa iyong backend.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Small-scale hardware example {#small-scale-hardware-example}"
msgstr "Small-scale na hardware example {#small-scale-hardware-example}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This section follows the four-step workflow on a QPU, using the same backend and the same\n"
"gate budget as the large-scale runs. The smaller problem provides an exact reference for checking the result.\n"
msgstr "Sinusundan ng seksyong ito ang four-step workflow sa isang QPU, gamit ang parehong backend at parehong gate budget gaya ng mga large-scale na run. Ang mas maliit na problema ay nagbibigay ng exact na reference para i-check ang resulta.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The small-scale problem is $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$: two valence protons and two valence neutrons in the\n"
"$sd$ shell above an $^{16}\\mathrm{O}$ core, with the USDA interaction [\\[2\\]](#references). Three\n"
"orbitals per species give 24 qubits, and the complete symmetry-allowed basis is 640 determinants,\n"
"small enough to compare the energy estimates with the exact answer.\n"
msgstr "Ang small-scale na problema ay ang $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$: dalawang valence proton at dalawang valence neutron sa $sd$ shell sa itaas ng $^{16}\\mathrm{O}$ core, na may USDA interaction [\\[2\\]](#references). Ang tatlong orbital bawat species ay nagbibigay ng 24 qubit, at ang kumpletong basis na pinapayagan ng symmetry ay 640 determinant, na sapat na maliit para ihambing ang mga energy estimate sa eksaktong sagot.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Map classical inputs to a quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"
msgstr "Step 1: I-map ang mga classical input sa isang quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Read the interaction, build the register, and construct the reference determinant. The following table shows the register information from the [Background](#background), read directly\n"
"from the interaction file.\n"
msgstr "Basahin ang interaction, buuin ang register, at buuin ang reference determinant. Ipinapakita ng sumusunod na table ang impormasyon ng register mula sa [Background](#background), na binasa nang direkta mula sa interaction file.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Run two checks on the Hamiltonian before continuing. Both are inexpensive and can reveal\n"
"recoupling errors that a single energy calculation might not detect.\n"
msgstr "Magpatakbo ng dalawang check sa Hamiltonian bago magpatuloy. Parehong mura ang mga ito at maaaring maglantad ng mga recoupling error na maaaring hindi matukoy ng isang energy calculation lamang.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A rotationally invariant Hamiltonian organizes its eigenstates into $J$ multiplets, so every\n"
"eigenvalue of the $M_J = 2$ sector must also appear in the $M_J = 0$ spectrum at the same energy. The gap between the ground state and the lowest state carrying $M_J = 2$ is the $2^+$ excitation\n"
"energy, which is measured: $1.634$ MeV for $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$ [\\[6\\]](#references). An empirical\n"
"$sd$-shell interaction is expected to agree within a few hundred keV.\n"
msgstr "Inaayos ng isang rotationally invariant na Hamiltonian ang mga eigenstate nito sa mga $J$ multiplet, kaya ang bawat eigenvalue ng $M_J = 2$ sector ay dapat ding lumitaw sa $M_J = 0$ spectrum sa parehong energy. Ang agwat sa pagitan ng ground state at ng pinakamababang state na may $M_J = 2$ ay ang $2^+$ excitation energy, na nasukat: $1.634$ MeV para sa $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$ [\\[6\\]](#references). Inaasahang tutugma ang isang empirical na $sd$-shell interaction sa loob ng ilang daang keV.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, construct the operator pool. Applying the two selection rules gives an important result: for this reference, in this model space, **there are no allowed single excitations at all**.\n"
msgstr "Susunod, buuin ang operator pool. Ang paglalapat ng dalawang selection rule ay nagbibigay ng mahalagang resulta: para sa reference na ito, sa model space na ito, **walang anumang pinapayagang single excitation**.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The reason is specific and checkable. A $1p1h$ excitation conserves $M_J$ only if the particle state\n"
"has the same $m_j$ as the hole. The reference occupies the two states of largest $|m_j|$ in the\n"
"lowest orbital ($m_j = \\pm 5/2$ of $0d_{5/2}$), and no other orbital in the $sd$ shell reaches\n"
"$|m_j| = 5/2$, since $0d_{3/2}$ stops at $3/2$ and $1s_{1/2}$ at $1/2$. Therefore, no single excitation\n"
"survives, and correlation is carried entirely by $2p2h$ excitations. This is a property of the\n"
"reference and the shell, not a general law; the following cell counts it rather than assuming it.\n"
msgstr "Tiyak at matsetsek ang dahilan. Ang $1p1h$ excitation ay nagko-conserve ng $M_J$ lamang kung ang particle state ay may parehong $m_j$ gaya ng hole. Inookupa ng reference ang dalawang state na may pinakamalaking $|m_j|$ sa pinakamababang orbital ($m_j = \\pm 5/2$ ng $0d_{5/2}$), at wala nang ibang orbital sa $sd$ shell ang umaabot sa $|m_j| = 5/2$, dahil ang $0d_{3/2}$ ay humihinto sa $3/2$ at ang $1s_{1/2}$ sa $1/2$. Samakatuwid, walang single excitation na nabubuhay, at ang correlation ay buong dala ng mga $2p2h$ excitation. Katangian ito ng reference at ng shell, hindi pangkalahatang batas; binibilang ito ng sumusunod na cell sa halip na ipagpalagay.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Optimize problem for quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"
msgstr "Step 2: I-optimize ang problema para sa quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Transpilation reveals the hardware cost of the Jordan-Wigner $Z$ strings and the savings from\n"
"using qubit excitations. The first cell measures both constructions against the real backend\n"
"target and checks the claim, introduced in the [Setup](#setup), that dropping the $Z$ strings changes the\n"
"amplitudes but not the set of determinants the circuit can reach.\n"
msgstr "Inilalantad ng transpilation ang hardware cost ng mga Jordan-Wigner $Z$ string at ang natitipid sa paggamit ng mga qubit excitation. Sinusukat ng unang cell ang parehong construction laban sa totoong backend target at tinitsek ang claim, na ipinakilala sa [Setup](#setup), na ang pag-alis ng mga $Z$ string ay nagbabago sa mga amplitude ngunit hindi sa set ng mga determinant na maaabot ng circuit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Compare two consequences of this substitution. A qubit excitation costs the same regardless of the distance between its\n"
"indices, so proton-neutron excitations, which span the boundary between the two halves of the\n"
"register and make up most of the pool, no longer have this additional cost. The whole pool then\n"
"fits inside the budget, which means the limit on the result is sampling rather than circuit depth.\n"
msgstr "Ihambing ang dalawang bunga ng pagpapalit na ito. Ang qubit excitation ay may parehong cost anuman ang distansya ng mga index nito, kaya ang mga proton-neutron excitation, na sumasaklaw sa hangganan ng dalawang kalahati ng register at bumubuo sa karamihan ng pool, ay wala nang karagdagang cost na ito. Kasya na ngayon ang buong pool sa loob ng budget, na nangangahulugang ang sampling na at hindi ang circuit depth ang limitasyon ng resulta.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Execute using Qiskit primitives {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives}"
msgstr "Step 3: Magsagawa gamit ang mga Qiskit primitive {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Submit one job per problem, with the whole ensemble as a single list of circuits. Gate and\n"
"measurement twirling and dynamical decoupling are enabled to reduce the effects of hardware noise.\n"
"Their benefit depends on the circuit and backend.\n"
msgstr "Magsumite ng isang job bawat problema, kung saan ang buong ensemble ay iisang listahan ng mga circuit. Naka-enable ang gate at measurement twirling at dynamical decoupling para mabawasan ang epekto ng hardware noise. Nakadepende sa circuit at backend ang benepisyo ng mga ito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Each job’s ID is printed. Use `service.job(\"JOB_ID\")` to retrieve the completed job and its\n"
"results without using additional QPU time.\n"
msgstr "Ipi-print ang ID ng bawat job. Gamitin ang `service.job(\"JOB_ID\")` para kunin ang natapos na job at ang mga resulta nito nang hindi gumagamit ng karagdagang QPU time.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4: Post-process and return result in desired classical format {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"
msgstr "Step 4: I-post-process at ibalik ang resulta sa nais na classical na format {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Convert the quantum samples into an energy estimate using the nuclear-symmetry constraints\n"
"described in the [Background](#background) section.\n"
msgstr "I-convert ang mga quantum sample sa isang energy estimate gamit ang mga nuclear-symmetry constraint na inilarawan sa seksyong [Background](#background).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Configuration recovery repairs the two nucleon numbers.** `recover_configurations` takes each shot that\n"
"has the wrong number of protons or neutrons and flips the bits least consistent with the current\n"
"estimate of the average orbital occupancies, instead of discarding it. On the first pass the\n"
"occupancy estimate comes from the shots that already survived; afterward it comes from the\n"
"eigenvector of the previous subspace, which makes the procedure self-consistent.\n"
msgstr "**Inaayos ng configuration recovery ang dalawang nucleon number.** Kinukuha ng `recover_configurations` ang bawat shot na may maling bilang ng proton o neutron at ini-flip ang mga bit na pinakamababa ang pagkakatugma sa kasalukuyang tantiya ng average na orbital occupancy, sa halip na itapon ito. Sa unang pass, ang occupancy estimate ay galing sa mga shot na nanatili na; pagkatapos nito, galing ito sa eigenvector ng nakaraang subspace, na nagpapa-self-consistent sa procedure.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**$M_J$ and parity are imposed on the recombined products, not on whole shots.** Every repaired shot\n"
"contributes a proton half and a neutron half, and the subspace is spanned by every product of a\n"
"sampled proton configuration with a sampled neutron configuration that lands at $M_J = 0$ with the\n"
"right parity. Filtering whole shots on total $M_J$ instead would throw away two good halves for the\n"
"sake of a quantum number that belongs to their combination.\n"
msgstr "**Ang $M_J$ at parity ay ipinapataw sa mga recombined na product, hindi sa buong shot.** Bawat naayos na shot ay nag-aambag ng proton half at neutron half, at ang subspace ay binubuo ng bawat product ng isang na-sample na proton configuration at isang na-sample na neutron configuration na napupunta sa $M_J = 0$ na may tamang parity. Ang pag-filter ng buong shot batay sa kabuuang $M_J$ ay magtatapon ng dalawang mahusay na half alang-alang sa isang quantum number na pag-aari ng kanilang kombinasyon.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The four quantum-number checks reject different fractions of samples. The two nucleon numbers\n"
"account for most of the filtering. Parity is *automatically* satisfied inside a single major shell: every $sd$ orbital\n"
"has even $\\ell$ and every $pf$ orbital odd $\\ell$, so once the nucleon numbers are right the parity\n"
"cannot be wrong. The parity check is retained because a cross-shell model space would make it an\n"
"independent constraint. The $M_J$ check keeps products in the target angular-momentum sector. The value of\n"
"having four exact quantum numbers is that they are *cheap and exact*, not that each one is a large\n"
"filter.\n"
msgstr "Ang apat na quantum-number check ay tumatanggi sa magkakaibang bahagi ng mga sample. Ang dalawang nucleon number ang bumubuo sa karamihan ng pag-filter. Ang parity ay *awtomatikong* nasisiyahan sa loob ng isang major shell: ang bawat $sd$ orbital ay may even na $\\ell$ at ang bawat $pf$ orbital ay odd na $\\ell$, kaya kapag tama na ang mga nucleon number, hindi na maaaring mali ang parity. Pinananatili ang parity check dahil gagawin itong independent na constraint ng isang cross-shell na model space. Pinananatili ng $M_J$ check ang mga product sa target na angular-momentum sector. Ang halaga ng pagkakaroon ng apat na eksaktong quantum number ay *mura at eksakto* ang mga ito, hindi dahil malaking filter ang bawat isa.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Diagonalizing gives a variational upper bound.** Because each iteration's subspace contains the\n"
"last, the sequence of energies falls monotonically, and every entry in it is a rigorous upper bound on\n"
"the true ground-state energy, regardless of the noise in the samples that produced it.\n"
msgstr "**Ang pag-diagonalize ay nagbibigay ng variational upper bound.** Dahil ang subspace ng bawat iteration ay naglalaman ng nauna, ang sequence ng mga energy ay bumababa nang monotone, at ang bawat entry rito ay isang mahigpit na upper bound sa tunay na ground-state energy, anuman ang noise sa mga sample na bumuo nito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Evaluate the results {#evaluate-the-results}"
msgstr "Suriin ang mga resulta {#evaluate-the-results}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use the following checks to evaluate your results on a Heron-class backend with these settings:\n"
msgstr "Gamitin ang mga sumusunod na pagsusuri para i-evaluate ang iyong mga resulta sa isang Heron-class backend gamit ang mga setting na ito:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Shot survival** on the two nucleon numbers measures the fraction of shots with the correct proton and neutron counts. It can fall as\n"
"the register grows. A survival rate near zero can indicate a problem with circuit execution. Check the ISA depth in Step 2 and the backend's calibration, not the post-processing.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang **shot survival** sa dalawang nucleon number ay sumusukat sa bahagi ng mga shot na may tamang bilang ng proton at neutron. Maaari itong bumaba habang\n"
"lumalaki ang register. Ang survival rate na malapit sa zero ay maaaring magpahiwatig ng problema sa pagpapatakbo ng circuit. Tingnan ang ISA depth sa Step 2 at ang calibration ng backend, hindi ang post-processing.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**The recovery loop** should print a subspace dimension that stays constant or grows and an energy that stays constant or falls with\n"
"each iteration. If iteration 1 already reaches `MAX_DIMENSION`, the classical solver rather than the\n"
"sampling is the binding constraint.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang **recovery loop** ay dapat mag-print ng subspace dimension na nananatiling pareho o lumalaki, at enerhiyang nananatiling pareho o bumababa sa\n"
"bawat iteration. Kung umaabot na sa `MAX_DIMENSION` ang iteration 1, ang classical solver at hindi ang\n"
"sampling ang naglilimita.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**The recovered fraction** for $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$ should be high, because the ansatz ceiling\n"
"computed in Step 1 is the full 640-determinant space; this run is where sampling, not\n"
"expressiveness, is the only obstacle.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang **recovered fraction** para sa $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$ ay dapat mataas, dahil ang ansatz ceiling\n"
"na kinompyut sa Step 1 ay ang buong 640-determinant na espasyo; sa run na ito, ang sampling, hindi ang\n"
"expressiveness, ang tanging hadlang.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**The two assertions** in the preceding cell check the variational bounds. A bound that rises means the\n"
"subspaces stopped being nested, and a bound below the exact energy means something is wrong with the\n"
"Hamiltonian, not with the hardware.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang **dalawang assertion** sa naunang cell ay nagsusuri ng mga variational bound. Ang bound na tumataas ay nangangahulugang hindi na\n"
"nested ang mga subspace, at ang bound na mas mababa sa eksaktong enerhiya ay nangangahulugang may mali sa\n"
"Hamiltonian, hindi sa hardware.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Counterintuitively, a *noisier* backend can give a slightly better bound than a clean one, because\n"
"errors produce valid half-configurations the ideal circuit would never have sampled, and widening\n"
"a variational subspace cannot raise its lowest eigenvalue. Noisy simulation can demonstrate the same effect; this tutorial shows it with\n"
"hardware samples.\n"
msgstr ""
"Taliwas sa inaasahan, ang *mas maingay* na backend ay maaaring magbigay ng bahagyang mas magandang bound kaysa sa malinis, dahil\n"
"ang mga error ay lumilikha ng mga valid na half-configuration na hindi kailanman masa-sample ng ideal na circuit, at ang pagpapalawak\n"
"ng variational subspace ay hindi makapagtataas sa pinakamababang eigenvalue nito. Maipapakita rin ito ng noisy simulation; ipinapakita ito ng tutorial na ito gamit ang\n"
"mga sample mula sa hardware.\n"

