msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/nuclear-sqd-pooled/extracted-outputs/c040-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Large-scale hardware example {#large-scale-hardware-example}"
msgstr "Halimbawa ng malakihang hardware {#large-scale-hardware-example}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Scaling up changes only the inputs, so the next step is to combine the four stages into one function\n"
"and run it twice, both times on a 40-qubit register in the $pf$ shell above a\n"
"$^{40}\\mathrm{Ca}$ core with the GXPF1 interaction [\\[3\\]](#references).\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang pag-scale up ay inputs lang ang binabago, kaya ang susunod na hakbang ay pagsamahin ang apat na stage sa isang function\n"
"at patakbuhin ito nang dalawang beses, parehong sa 40-qubit na register sa $pf$ shell sa ibabaw ng\n"
"$^{40}\\mathrm{Ca}$ core na may GXPF1 interaction [\\[3\\]](#references).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The two runs illustrate different aspects of scaling:\n"
msgstr "Ipinapakita ng dalawang run ang magkaibang aspeto ng scaling:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$^{44}\\mathrm{Ti}$, two valence protons and two valence neutrons, has a 4,000-determinant basis. The\n"
"register is 40 qubits, but the problem is still small enough to diagonalize exactly on a laptop, so\n"
"you can compare the hardware result with an exact reference after increasing the register size.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang $^{44}\\mathrm{Ti}$, na may dalawang valence proton at dalawang valence neutron, ay may 4,000-determinant na basis. Ang\n"
"register ay 40 qubit, pero sapat pa ring maliit ang problema para ma-diagonalize nang eksakto sa laptop, kaya\n"
"maihahambing mo ang resulta ng hardware sa eksaktong reference pagkatapos palakihin ang register.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$^{48}\\mathrm{Cr}$, four valence protons and four valence neutrons, has 1,963,461 symmetry-allowed determinants in the same 40 qubits.\n"
"The tutorial's dense solver cannot diagonalize that full space, so the run returns\n"
"a rigorous upper bound and the reference determinant it improves on.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang $^{48}\\mathrm{Cr}$, na may apat na valence proton at apat na valence neutron, ay may 1,963,461 symmetry-allowed na determinant sa parehong 40 qubit.\n"
"Hindi kayang i-diagonalize ng dense solver ng tutorial ang buong espasyong iyon, kaya ang run ay nagbabalik\n"
"ng mahigpit na upper bound at ng reference determinant na pinahuhusay nito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Watch two quantities across the two runs. The fraction of the pool that fits inside the fixed gate\n"
"budget shrinks as the pool grows, and `pack_ensemble` reports how much is included. The\n"
"subspace stops being limited by sampling and starts being limited by `MAX_DIMENSION`, the largest\n"
"matrix the dense classical solver here builds. At this scale, a production\n"
"calculation would use a selected configuration interaction (selected-CI) solver.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bantayan ang dalawang dami sa dalawang run. Ang bahagi ng pool na kasya sa nakapirming gate\n"
"budget ay lumiliit habang lumalaki ang pool, at iniuulat ng `pack_ensemble` kung gaano karami ang kasama. Ang\n"
"subspace ay hindi na nalilimitahan ng sampling at nalilimitahan na ng `MAX_DIMENSION`, ang pinakamalaking\n"
"matrix na kayang buuin ng dense classical solver dito. Sa ganitong laki, ang production\n"
"calculation ay gagamit ng selected configuration interaction (selected-CI) solver.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Combine steps 1–4 {#combine-steps-14}"
msgstr "Pagsamahin ang mga step 1–4 {#combine-steps-14}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following function calls the same stages as the walkthrough, in the same order.\n"
msgstr "Tinatawag ng sumusunod na function ang parehong mga stage tulad ng walkthrough, sa parehong pagkakasunod-sunod.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "$^{44}\\mathrm{Ti}$: the same workflow on a 40-qubit register {#44mathrmti-the-same-workflow-on-a-40-qubit-register}"
msgstr "$^{44}\\mathrm{Ti}$: ang parehong workflow sa 40-qubit na register {#44mathrmti-the-same-workflow-on-a-40-qubit-register}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The $pf$ shell above $^{40}\\mathrm{Ca}$ has four orbitals per species and 20 magnetic substates each,\n"
"so the register is 40 qubits. Two valence protons and two valence neutrons make $^{44}\\mathrm{Ti}$,\n"
"with 4,000 symmetry-allowed determinants &mdash; about six times the $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$ basis, using\n"
"40 qubits instead of 24.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang $pf$ shell sa ibabaw ng $^{40}\\mathrm{Ca}$ ay may apat na orbital bawat species at 20 magnetic substate bawat isa,\n"
"kaya ang register ay 40 qubit. Ang dalawang valence proton at dalawang valence neutron ay bumubuo sa $^{44}\\mathrm{Ti}$,\n"
"na may 4,000 symmetry-allowed na determinant &mdash; mga anim na beses ng basis ng $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$, gamit ang\n"
"40 qubit sa halip na 24.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is the larger of the two examples that the notebook can solve exactly, so you can compare\n"
"the hardware result with an exact reference.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ito ang mas malaki sa dalawang halimbawang kayang lutasin nang eksakto ng notebook, kaya maihahambing mo\n"
"ang resulta ng hardware sa eksaktong reference.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "$^{48}\\mathrm{Cr}$: beyond the tutorial's exact-diagonalization capacity {#48mathrmcr-beyond-the-tutorials-exact-diagonalization-capacity}"
msgstr "$^{48}\\mathrm{Cr}$: lampas sa kapasidad ng exact diagonalization ng tutorial {#48mathrmcr-beyond-the-tutorials-exact-diagonalization-capacity}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Adding two protons and two neutrons uses the same 40-qubit register (`4, 4` for\n"
"$^{48}\\mathrm{Cr}$) and increases the basis size by a factor of about 491, to 1,963,461 symmetry-allowed determinants. That\n"
"matrix is far beyond anything this tutorial will build, so `exact=False`: there is no exact reference energy,\n"
"only the variational bound and the reference determinant it improves on.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang pagdaragdag ng dalawang proton at dalawang neutron ay gumagamit ng parehong 40-qubit na register (`4, 4` para sa\n"
"$^{48}\\mathrm{Cr}$) at nagpapalaki sa basis nang humigit-kumulang 491 beses, hanggang 1,963,461 symmetry-allowed na determinant. Ang\n"
"matrix na iyon ay malayong lampas sa kayang buuin ng tutorial na ito, kaya `exact=False`: walang eksaktong reference na enerhiya,\n"
"tanging ang variational bound at ang reference determinant na pinahuhusay nito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Two things change at this scale, and both are visible in the printout. The pool grows to several\n"
"hundred allowed excitations, so the fixed gate budget now covers a minority of it rather than all of\n"
"it. Also, the product subspace the samples span is larger than `MAX_DIMENSION`, so the dense solver\n"
"truncates it by sampled weight. The bound remains rigorous but can be less accurate than a bound\n"
"computed from all the sampled configurations. A production calculation would retain the samples\n"
"and use a solver that supports a larger subspace.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalawang bagay ang nagbabago sa ganitong laki, at pareho itong nakikita sa printout. Ang pool ay lumalaki hanggang sa ilang\n"
"daang allowed na excitation, kaya ang nakapirming gate budget ay sumasaklaw na lang sa maliit na bahagi nito sa halip na sa lahat\n"
"ng ito. Gayundin, ang product subspace na sakop ng mga sample ay mas malaki kaysa sa `MAX_DIMENSION`, kaya ang dense solver ay\n"
"nagpuputol nito ayon sa sampled weight. Nananatiling mahigpit ang bound pero maaaring hindi gaanong tumpak kaysa sa bound na\n"
"kinompyut mula sa lahat ng na-sample na configuration. Ang production calculation ay magpapanatili ng mga sample\n"
"at gagamit ng solver na sumusuporta sa mas malaking subspace.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Evaluate a result without an exact reference {#evaluate-a-result-without-an-exact-reference}"
msgstr "Suriin ang resulta nang walang eksaktong reference {#evaluate-a-result-without-an-exact-reference}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The $^{48}\\mathrm{Cr}$ run has no exact reference within this tutorial. Use the existing samples\n"
"to assess convergence and compare with the classical selection baseline, without additional QPU\n"
"time or full-space diagonalization.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang run ng $^{48}\\mathrm{Cr}$ ay walang eksaktong reference sa loob ng tutorial na ito. Gamitin ang mga umiiral na sample\n"
"para tasahin ang convergence at ihambing sa classical selection baseline, nang walang karagdagang QPU\n"
"time o full-space diagonalization.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Is it converged?** Reorder the retained determinants by their weight in the converged eigenvector\n"
"and the subspaces become *nested*, so diagonalizing the leading $d \\times d$ block for a ladder of $d$\n"
"traces the bound's descent across two decades of subspace size. If it is still falling steeply at the\n"
"largest $d$, the classical solver's dimension cap is the binding constraint and `MAX_DIMENSION` is the\n"
"parameter to increase. If it has flattened, adding more of the retained determinants offers little improvement;\n"
"further progress may require sampling additional configurations. The\n"
"Hamiltonian is built once at full size and every rung is a principal block of it, so the whole\n"
"sweep costs one matrix build rather than one per rung.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Converged na ba?** Muling ayusin ang mga napanatiling determinant ayon sa bigat nila sa converged na eigenvector\n"
"at magiging *nested* ang mga subspace, kaya ang pag-diagonalize sa nangungunang $d \\times d$ na block para sa isang hanay ng $d$\n"
"ay susubaybay sa pagbaba ng bound sa dalawang dekada ng laki ng subspace. Kung matarik pa rin ang pagbaba sa\n"
"pinakamalaking $d$, ang dimension cap ng classical solver ang naglilimita at ang `MAX_DIMENSION` ang\n"
"parameter na dapat dagdagan. Kung pumatag na, kaunti na lang ang naidadagdag ng karagdagang mga napanatiling determinant;\n"
"maaaring mangailangan ng pag-sample ng karagdagang configuration para umusad pa. Ang\n"
"Hamiltonian ay binubuo nang isang beses sa buong laki at bawat rung ay principal block nito, kaya ang buong\n"
"sweep ay isang matrix build lang sa halip na isa bawat rung.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**How does quantum sampling compare with classical selection?** Compare with a subspace of the\n"
"same size chosen by the classical selection procedure: take the pool ranked by perturbation theory in score\n"
"order, grow the product subspace to the same dimension, and diagonalize that instead. Both curves are\n"
"rigorous upper bounds on the same Hamiltonian, so whichever sits lower at equal dimension picked the\n"
"better determinants. This comparison decides whether hardware sampling improves the energy estimate\n"
"relative to this classical baseline.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Paano ihahambing ang quantum sampling sa classical selection?** Ihambing sa subspace na\n"
"pareho ang laki na pinili ng classical selection procedure: kunin ang pool na naka-rank ayon sa perturbation theory sa pagkakasunod-sunod ng\n"
"score, palakihin ang product subspace hanggang sa parehong dimension, at i-diagonalize iyon sa halip. Parehong mahigpit\n"
"na upper bound ang dalawang curve sa iisang Hamiltonian, kaya alinman ang mas mababa sa magkapantay na dimension ay pumili ng\n"
"mas magagandang determinant. Ang paghahambing na ito ang magpapasya kung pinahuhusay ng hardware sampling ang energy estimate\n"
"kumpara sa classical baseline na ito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This subspace is not selected for excited states. Configuration recovery steers the subspace\n"
"using ground-state occupancies, so the higher eigenvalues are much further from converged than the\n"
"lowest one, and the first excitation energy comes out well above the measured $2^+$. Reaching excited\n"
"states properly needs a subspace selected for them.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang subspace na ito ay hindi piniling para sa mga excited state. Ang configuration recovery ay gumagabay sa subspace\n"
"gamit ang mga ground-state occupancy, kaya ang mas matataas na eigenvalue ay mas malayo sa converged kaysa sa\n"
"pinakamababa, at ang unang excitation energy ay lumalabas na mas mataas nang husto kaysa sa nasukat na $2^+$. Para maabot nang maayos ang mga excited\n"
"state, kailangan ng subspace na piniling para sa kanila.\n"

