# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Summary {#summary}"
msgstr "Buod {#summary}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"One workflow, unchanged apart from its inputs, ran on a QPU at three problem sizes: a 24-qubit\n"
"problem you can check exactly, a 40-qubit problem you can still check exactly, and a 40-qubit problem\n"
"with nearly two million basis states beyond this tutorial's exact-diagonalization capacity.\n"
msgstr ""
"Isang workflow, hindi nagbago maliban sa mga input nito, ang tumakbo sa isang QPU sa tatlong laki ng problema: isang 24-qubit\n"
"na problemang maaari mong suriin nang eksakto, isang 40-qubit na problemang maaari mo pa ring suriin nang eksakto, at isang 40-qubit na problema\n"
"na may halos dalawang milyong basis state, lampas sa kapasidad ng exact diagonalization ng tutorial na ito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The three runs illustrate the following points:\n"
msgstr "Ipinapakita ng tatlong run ang mga sumusunod na punto:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**The quantum step only has to propose determinants.** The circuit is fixed, seeded from\n"
"second-order perturbation theory, and never optimized. Nothing in the workflow needs its amplitudes\n"
"to be accurate, only its support to be useful. Classical diagonalization in the selected subspace gives a\n"
"variational upper bound, although the bound varies with the sampled configurations.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Ang quantum step ay kailangan lang magmungkahi ng mga determinant.** Ang circuit ay nakapirmi, binuo mula sa\n"
"second-order perturbation theory, at hindi kailanman ino-optimize. Walang bahagi ng workflow ang nangangailangan na tumpak ang mga amplitude nito,\n"
"tanging na kapaki-pakinabang ang support nito. Ang classical diagonalization sa napiling subspace ay nagbibigay ng\n"
"variational upper bound, bagaman nag-iiba ang bound ayon sa mga na-sample na configuration.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Qubit excitations reduce circuit depth.** Because only the support matters, the fermionic excitation blocks\n"
"can be replaced by qubit excitations, whose cost does not grow with the distance between the\n"
"orbitals they connect. Step 2 measured the saving on the actual backend, which is the difference\n"
"between a circuit that fits comfortably inside coherence and one that does not.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Binabawasan ng mga qubit excitation ang circuit depth.** Dahil ang support lang ang mahalaga, ang mga fermionic excitation block\n"
"ay maaaring palitan ng mga qubit excitation, na ang gastos ay hindi lumalaki sa layo ng mga\n"
"orbital na kinokonekta nila. Sinukat ng Step 2 ang natipid sa aktwal na backend, na siyang pagkakaiba\n"
"ng circuit na kasya nang maluwag sa loob ng coherence at ng hindi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Configuration recovery reuses noisy samples.** Every shot with the wrong proton or neutron number is repaired\n"
"against the current occupancy estimate rather than discarded, and each repaired half-configuration\n"
"can add configurations to the subspace. Widening a variational subspace cannot raise its lowest\n"
"eigenvalue. This tutorial demonstrates configuration recovery using hardware samples.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Muling ginagamit ng configuration recovery ang mga maingay na sample.** Ang bawat shot na may maling bilang ng proton o neutron ay inaayos\n"
"batay sa kasalukuyang occupancy estimate sa halip na itapon, at ang bawat naayos na half-configuration\n"
"ay maaaring magdagdag ng mga configuration sa subspace. Ang pagpapalawak ng variational subspace ay hindi makapagtataas sa pinakamababang\n"
"eigenvalue nito. Ipinapakita ng tutorial na ito ang configuration recovery gamit ang mga sample mula sa hardware.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**The binding constraint moves as you scale.** At 24 qubits the ansatz could reach the exact answer,\n"
"and only sampling stood in the way. At 40 qubits with four valence nucleons per species, the gate\n"
"budget covers a minority of the pool and the dense classical solver caps the subspace. Knowing which\n"
"of the three is limiting you is the practical skill this workflow teaches.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Gumagalaw ang binding constraint habang nag-i-scale ka.** Sa 24 qubit, kaya ng ansatz na maabot ang eksaktong sagot,\n"
"at sampling lang ang humahadlang. Sa 40 qubit na may apat na valence nucleon bawat species, ang gate\n"
"budget ay sumasaklaw sa maliit na bahagi ng pool at nililimitahan ng dense classical solver ang subspace. Ang pag-alam kung alin\n"
"sa tatlo ang naglilimita sa iyo ang praktikal na kasanayang itinuturo ng workflow na ito.\n"

