# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Extensions to consider {#extensions-to-consider}"
msgstr "Mga extension na dapat isaalang-alang {#extensions-to-consider}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Replace the dense solver.** `MAX_DIMENSION` is the ceiling on everything at the $^{48}\\mathrm{Cr}$\n"
"scale, and `np.linalg.eigh` on a dense matrix is why. Building the same projected\n"
"Hamiltonian as a sparse matrix and using an iterative eigensolver such as\n"
"`scipy.sparse.linalg.eigsh`, or a Davidson or selected-CI solver designed for nuclear two-body\n"
"interactions, could support larger subspaces. The practical limit depends on matrix sparsity,\n"
"available memory, and solver convergence, and this tutorial does not benchmark that extension. The SQD addon's `qiskit_addon_sqd.fermion.solve_sci` is not a drop-in substitute: it wraps an\n"
"electronic-structure solver and expects one- and two-body integrals in that form, so the shared\n"
"proton $\\times$ neutron product structure is not sufficient on its own. Using it would mean mapping\n"
"the shell-model interaction of Equation (1) into those integrals and validating the result against the\n"
"exact energies this notebook already computes.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Palitan ang dense solver.** Ang `MAX_DIMENSION` ang hangganan ng lahat sa sukat ng $^{48}\\mathrm{Cr}$,\n"
"at ang `np.linalg.eigh` sa dense matrix ang dahilan nito. Ang pagbuo ng parehong projected\n"
"Hamiltonian bilang sparse matrix at paggamit ng iterative eigensolver gaya ng\n"
"`scipy.sparse.linalg.eigsh`, o ng Davidson o selected-CI solver na dinisenyo para sa nuclear two-body\n"
"interaction, ay maaaring sumuporta sa mas malalaking subspace. Ang praktikal na limitasyon ay nakasalalay sa sparsity ng matrix,\n"
"magagamit na memory, at convergence ng solver, at hindi bini-benchmark ng tutorial na ito ang extension na iyon. Ang `qiskit_addon_sqd.fermion.solve_sci` ng SQD addon ay hindi basta-bastang kapalit: bumabalot ito sa isang\n"
"electronic-structure solver at inaasahan ang one- at two-body integral sa anyong iyon, kaya ang pinagsasaluhang\n"
"proton $\\times$ neutron product structure ay hindi sapat nang mag-isa. Ang paggamit nito ay mangangahulugan ng pag-map\n"
"sa shell-model interaction ng Equation (1) sa mga integral na iyon at pag-validate ng resulta laban sa\n"
"mga eksaktong enerhiyang kinokompyut na ng notebook na ito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Add batching and subsampling.** The published pooled SQD workflow diagonalizes several independent\n"
"subsamples per iteration and keeps the best. This tutorial uses one batch per iteration, which is\n"
"harmless for the variational bound but does not provide the variance information that indicates whether more shots\n"
"would help.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Magdagdag ng batching at subsampling.** Ang nailathalang pooled SQD workflow ay nagdi-diagonalize ng ilang independent na\n"
"subsample bawat iteration at pinapanatili ang pinakamahusay. Ang tutorial na ito ay gumagamit ng isang batch bawat iteration, na\n"
"hindi nakakasama sa variational bound pero hindi nagbibigay ng variance information na nagpapahiwatig kung makakatulong ba ang mas maraming\n"
"shot.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Excited states and other sectors.** The higher eigenvalues of each subspace Hamiltonian are upper\n"
"bounds on excited states in the same symmetry sector, and running at $M_J \\neq 0$ reaches other\n"
"sectors. The $2^+$ check in Step 1 is already half of this calculation.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Mga excited state at iba pang sector.** Ang mas matataas na eigenvalue ng bawat subspace Hamiltonian ay mga upper\n"
"bound sa mga excited state sa parehong symmetry sector, at ang pagpapatakbo sa $M_J \\neq 0$ ay umaabot sa iba pang\n"
"sector. Ang $2^+$ check sa Step 1 ay kalahati na ng kalkulasyong ito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**A cross-shell model space.** Parity is automatically satisfied inside a single major shell, which\n"
"is why it does no work here. An $sd$-$pf$ space mixes $\\ell$ parities, making parity a genuine\n"
"fourth constraint, one that neither SQD's Hamming-weight repair nor the product\n"
"construction would catch on its own.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Isang cross-shell na model space.** Awtomatikong nasasapatan ang parity sa loob ng iisang major shell, kaya\n"
"walang trabahong ginagawa ito rito. Ang $sd$-$pf$ na espasyo ay naghahalo ng mga $\\ell$ parity, kaya ang parity ay nagiging tunay na\n"
"ikaapat na constraint, na hindi makikita ng Hamming-weight repair ng SQD o ng product\n"
"construction nang mag-isa.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Odd-mass nuclei.** `reference_determinant` requires an even valence count in each species,\n"
"because a time-reversed paired filling is what forces $M_J = 0$. An odd nucleus needs a\n"
"half-integer $M_J$ target and an unpaired reference.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Mga nucleus na may odd na mass.** Ang `reference_determinant` ay nangangailangan ng even na bilang ng valence sa bawat species,\n"
"dahil ang time-reversed paired filling ang nagpapatupad ng $M_J = 0$. Ang odd na nucleus ay nangangailangan ng\n"
"half-integer na $M_J$ target at unpaired na reference.\n"

