msgstr "Appendix {#appendix}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This section explains the reasoning behind the helpers introduced in the [Setup](#setup) section.\n"
msgstr "Ipinapaliwanag ng seksyong ito ang katwiran sa likod ng mga helper na ipinakilala sa seksyong [Setup](#setup).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Why the mass-dependence rescaling is not optional {#why-the-mass-dependence-rescaling-is-not-optional}"
msgstr "Bakit hindi opsyonal ang mass-dependence rescaling {#why-the-mass-dependence-rescaling-is-not-optional}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Empirical shell-model interactions are fitted at one mass and applied across a chain of isotopes, with\n"
"the two-body matrix elements scaled as $(A/A_{\\mathrm{ref}})^{p}$. Both interaction files carry\n"
"$p = -0.3$, with $A_{\\mathrm{ref}} = 18$ for the USD family and $42$ for GXPF1. On the two-body header\n"
"line of a `.snt` file, those two numbers sit where an oscillator frequency and a core energy would\n"
"plausibly go, which makes them easy to misread; reading the exponent as a constant core energy adds a\n"
"spurious offset to every diagonal element *and* drops the rescaling, changing the correlation energy by\n"
"a few percent. The symmetry check in Step 1 does not by itself verify the energy scale. Comparing\n"
"the $2^+$ excitation energy, measured in MeV, with experiment provides an additional check on the\n"
"mass-dependent rescaling. An excitation energy is a difference between levels, so it does not\n"
"detect a constant offset applied to all energies.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga empirical shell-model interaction ay fina-fit sa isang mass at inilalapat sa isang chain ng mga isotope, kung saan ang\n"
"mga two-body matrix element ay sina-scale bilang $(A/A_{\\mathrm{ref}})^{p}$. Parehong may dala ang dalawang interaction file ng\n"
"$p = -0.3$, na may $A_{\\mathrm{ref}} = 18$ para sa USD family at $42$ para sa GXPF1. Sa two-body header\n"
"line ng isang `.snt` file, ang dalawang numerong iyon ay nasa lugar kung saan karaniwang inilalagay ang oscillator frequency at core energy,\n"
"kaya madali silang mabasa nang mali; ang pagbasa sa exponent bilang constant na core energy ay nagdaragdag ng\n"
"hindi totoong offset sa bawat diagonal element *at* nag-aalis ng rescaling, na nagbabago sa correlation energy nang\n"
"ilang porsyento. Hindi nito mismong bine-verify ng symmetry check sa Step 1 ang energy scale. Ang paghahambing\n"
"ng $2^+$ excitation energy, na sinusukat sa MeV, sa eksperimento ay nagbibigay ng karagdagang pagsusuri sa\n"
"mass-dependent na rescaling. Ang excitation energy ay pagkakaiba sa pagitan ng mga level, kaya hindi nito\n"
"natutukoy ang constant offset na inilapat sa lahat ng enerhiya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Why the reference is found by search rather than by filling {#why-the-reference-is-found-by-search-rather-than-by-filling}"
msgstr "Bakit hinahanap sa pamamagitan ng search ang reference at hindi sa pamamagitan ng filling {#why-the-reference-is-found-by-search-rather-than-by-filling}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The obvious reference is the determinant that fills the lowest single-particle energies. It is not the\n"
"lowest-energy determinant, because the diagonal of Equation (1) includes the two-body term\n"
"$\\sum_{i<j} \\langle ij \\| ij \\rangle$, and the pairing interaction strongly prefers occupying\n"
"time-reversed $(+m_j, -m_j)$ partners in the *largest* available $|m_j|$. In the $sd$ shell that is the\n"
"difference between the $m_j = \\pm 1/2$ pair and the $m_j = \\pm 5/2$ pair of $0d_{5/2}$, and it is worth\n"
"about 1 MeV; in the $pf$ shell, it is worth closer to 2. Because the reference energy defines the zero of the\n"
"\"correlation energy recovered\" metric, a poor choice inflates that metric and gives a less accurate\n"
"starting point.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang halatang reference ay ang determinant na pumupuno sa pinakamababang single-particle energy. Hindi ito ang\n"
"determinant na may pinakamababang enerhiya, dahil ang diagonal ng Equation (1) ay kasama ang two-body term\n"
"$\\sum_{i<j} \\langle ij \\| ij \\rangle$, at malakas na mas gusto ng pairing interaction ang pag-okupa sa\n"
"mga time-reversed na $(+m_j, -m_j)$ partner sa *pinakamalaking* magagamit na $|m_j|$. Sa $sd$ shell, iyon ang\n"
"pagkakaiba ng $m_j = \\pm 1/2$ na pares at ng $m_j = \\pm 5/2$ na pares ng $0d_{5/2}$, at nagkakahalaga ito ng\n"
"humigit-kumulang 1 MeV; sa $pf$ shell, mas malapit ito sa 2. Dahil ang reference energy ang nagtatakda ng zero ng\n"
"metric na \"correlation energy recovered\", ang hindi magandang pagpili ay nagpapalobo sa metric na iyon at nagbibigay ng mas hindi tumpak na\n"
"panimulang punto.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Restricting to paired fillings makes exhaustive search inexpensive, with $\\binom{n_{\\mathrm{pairs}}}{k}$ candidates per\n"
"species (a few thousand at most), and ensures $M_J = 0$. In every case in this\n"
"tutorial that can be checked against a full enumeration, the search returns the global lowest-diagonal\n"
"determinant, which is also the single largest component of the exact ground state.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang paghihigpit sa mga paired filling ay ginagawang mura ang exhaustive search, na may $\\binom{n_{\\mathrm{pairs}}}{k}$ na kandidato bawat\n"
"species (ilang libo ang pinakamarami), at tinitiyak ang $M_J = 0$. Sa bawat kasong\n"
"sa tutorial na ito na maaaring suriin laban sa buong enumeration, ibinabalik ng search ang global na determinant na may pinakamababang diagonal,\n"
"na siya ring pinakamalaking bahagi ng eksaktong ground state.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Why the first-order amplitude, not the exact two-level angle {#why-the-first-order-amplitude-not-the-exact-two-level-angle}"
msgstr "Bakit ang first-order amplitude, hindi ang eksaktong two-level angle {#why-the-first-order-amplitude-not-the-exact-two-level-angle}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Diagonalizing the $2 \\times 2$ Hamiltonian in the space\n"
"$\\{|\\Phi_{\\mathrm{ref}}\\rangle, |\\alpha\\rangle\\}$ gives the mixing angle\n"
"$\\theta_{\\mathrm{exact}} = \\tfrac{1}{2}\\arctan(2V/\\Delta)$; it might be tempting to call that the correct\n"
"choice for an *isolated* pair of levels. In this ansatz, several dozen excitation blocks act\n"
"in sequence on the same reference, so optimizing each block separately does not necessarily\n"
"optimize the composite circuit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang pag-diagonalize sa $2 \\times 2$ Hamiltonian sa espasyong\n"
"$\\{|\\Phi_{\\mathrm{ref}}\\rangle, |\\alpha\\rangle\\}$ ay nagbibigay ng mixing angle na\n"
"$\\theta_{\\mathrm{exact}} = \\tfrac{1}{2}\\arctan(2V/\\Delta)$; maaaring matuksong tawagin itong tamang\n"
"pagpili para sa *nakahiwalay* na pares ng mga level. Sa ansatz na ito, ilang dosenang excitation block ang kumikilos\n"
"nang sunud-sunod sa iisang reference, kaya ang pag-optimize sa bawat block nang hiwalay ay hindi kinakailangang\n"
"mag-optimize sa composite na circuit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The circuit’s role determines the choice of angle. Since\n"
"$|\\tfrac{1}{2}\\arctan(2x)| \\le |x|$ for every real $x$, the exact angle is always *smaller* in\n"
"magnitude than the first-order amplitude $t = V/\\Delta$, and therefore always leaves *more* amplitude\n"
"on the reference determinant. A circuit that keeps more amplitude on the reference returns the\n"
"reference more often and distinct excited determinants less often. For pooled SQD, the useful output of a shot\n"
"is a determinant the classical step has not seen yet, which motivates using the larger angle in this tutorial. Neither angle needs to be accurate, because the classical diagonalization discards the circuit's\n"
"amplitudes entirely and re-derives its own.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang papel ng circuit ang tumutukoy sa pagpili ng angle. Dahil\n"
"$|\\tfrac{1}{2}\\arctan(2x)| \\le |x|$ para sa bawat real na $x$, ang eksaktong angle ay laging *mas maliit* sa\n"
"magnitude kaysa sa first-order amplitude na $t = V/\\Delta$, at samakatuwid ay laging nag-iiwan ng *mas maraming* amplitude\n"
"sa reference determinant. Ang circuit na nagpapanatili ng mas maraming amplitude sa reference ay mas madalas na ibinabalik ang\n"
"reference at mas madalang ang mga natatanging excited determinant. Para sa pooled SQD, ang kapaki-pakinabang na output ng isang shot\n"
"ay determinant na hindi pa nakikita ng classical step, na siyang dahilan ng paggamit ng mas malaking angle sa tutorial na ito. Hindi kailangang maging tumpak ang alinmang angle, dahil itinatapon nang buo ng classical diagonalization ang mga\n"
"amplitude ng circuit at kinukuha ang sarili nitong mga amplitude.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Why pooled SQD can use qubit excitations {#why-pooled-sqd-can-use-qubit-excitations}"
msgstr "Bakit magagamit ng pooled SQD ang mga qubit excitation {#why-pooled-sqd-can-use-qubit-excitations}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The fermionic excitation $T = a_{v_1}^\\dagger a_{v_2}^\\dagger a_{h_2} a_{h_1}$ maps under\n"
"Jordan-Wigner to eight Pauli strings, each carrying $Z$ operators on every qubit between the outermost\n"
"indices. Those strings encode the fermionic sign, and their cost grows with the span, which for a\n"
"proton-neutron excitation is the whole register.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang fermionic excitation na $T = a_{v_1}^\\dagger a_{v_2}^\\dagger a_{h_2} a_{h_1}$ ay nagma-map sa ilalim ng\n"
"Jordan-Wigner tungo sa walong Pauli string, na bawat isa ay may dalang $Z$ operator sa bawat qubit sa pagitan ng pinakalabas na\n"
"mga index. Ang mga string na iyon ang nag-e-encode ng fermionic sign, at lumalaki ang gastos nila ayon sa span, na para sa\n"
"proton-neutron excitation ay ang buong register.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Deleting them gives the qubit-excitation operator of Yordanov et al. [\\[5\\]](#references). It is a\n"
"different operator: the state it prepares differs from the fermionic one in the *signs* of\n"
"its amplitudes, and the two sampling distributions can differ substantially. What it does not change\n"
"is which determinants have nonzero amplitude, because each block still rotates within the same\n"
"two-dimensional space $\\{|d\\rangle, |d'\\rangle\\}$ for every determinant $d$ it acts on, and it still\n"
"conserves both nucleon numbers, $M_J$, and parity exactly. The reachable set of determinants is\n"
"therefore identical, and the reachable set is the only thing pooled SQD uses; the classical\n"
"diagonalization assigns its own amplitudes regardless. Step 2 verifies the identical-support claim on\n"
"a real operator from the pool and measures what the substitution saves.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang pagtanggal sa mga iyon ay nagbibigay ng qubit-excitation operator ni Yordanov et al. [\\[5\\]](#references). Ito ay\n"
"ibang operator: ang state na inihahanda nito ay naiiba sa fermionic sa mga *sign* ng\n"
"mga amplitude nito, at ang dalawang sampling distribution ay maaaring magkaiba nang malaki. Ang hindi nito binabago\n"
"ay kung aling mga determinant ang may nonzero na amplitude, dahil ang bawat block ay umiikot pa rin sa loob ng parehong\n"
"two-dimensional na espasyong $\\{|d\\rangle, |d'\\rangle\\}$ para sa bawat determinant na $d$ na kinikilusan nito, at pinapanatili pa rin nito nang eksakto\n"
"ang parehong nucleon number, ang $M_J$, at ang parity. Ang reachable set ng mga determinant ay\n"
"samakatuwid ay magkapareho, at ang reachable set ang tanging ginagamit ng pooled SQD; ang classical\n"
"diagonalization ay nagtatakda ng sarili nitong mga amplitude anuman. Bine-verify ng Step 2 ang pag-aangking magkapareho ang support sa\n"
"isang tunay na operator mula sa pool at sinusukat kung ano ang natitipid ng pagpapalit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The limitation is that the sampling *weights* differ, so the two constructions will not discover\n"
"determinants in the same order at finite shot count. Since the ranking that decides which excitations\n"
"enter the circuits is classical and unchanged, and the classical step re-weights everything anyway,\n"
"the difference in sampling weights is a tradeoff for reduced circuit depth.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang limitasyon ay magkaiba ang mga *weight* ng sampling, kaya hindi madidiskubre ng dalawang konstruksyon ang mga\n"
"determinant sa parehong pagkakasunod-sunod sa may hangganang bilang ng shot. Dahil ang ranking na nagpapasya kung aling mga excitation\n"
"ang papasok sa mga circuit ay classical at hindi nagbabago, at muling tinitimbang ng classical step ang lahat pa rin,\n"
"ang pagkakaiba sa mga sampling weight ay isang tradeoff para sa nabawasang circuit depth.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Why $M_J$ belongs to the product stage {#why-m-j-belongs-to-the-product-stage}"
msgstr "Bakit ang $M_J$ ay nabibilang sa product stage {#why-m-j-belongs-to-the-product-stage}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Post-selection and configuration recovery both act on Hamming weights: the number of protons in one\n"
"half of the register, and the number of neutrons in the other. $M_J = M_p + M_n$ is not of that form. It is a property of a proton configuration *paired with* a neutron configuration. A shot whose proton\n"
"half and neutron half each carry the right nucleon number contains two usable half-configurations even\n"
"when their $M_J$ values do not cancel, because the proton half at $M_p = +1$ is perfectly good once it\n"
"is paired with a neutron half at $M_n = -1$. Filtering whole shots on total $M_J$ throws both halves\n"
"away, and imposing $M_J$ on the recombined products keeps them. The same argument explains why\n"
"`recover_configurations` needs no notion of $M_J$ to be useful in this case.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang post-selection at configuration recovery ay parehong kumikilos sa mga Hamming weight: ang bilang ng proton sa isang\n"
"halves ng register, at ang bilang ng neutron sa kabila. Ang $M_J = M_p + M_n$ ay hindi ganoong anyo. Ito ay katangian ng isang proton configuration na *ipinares sa* isang neutron configuration. Ang shot na ang proton\n"
"half at neutron half ay parehong may tamang nucleon number ay naglalaman ng dalawang magagamit na half-configuration kahit\n"
"hindi nagkakansela ang mga $M_J$ value nila, dahil ang proton half sa $M_p = +1$ ay perpektong maganda kapag\n"
"ipinares sa neutron half sa $M_n = -1$. Ang pag-filter sa buong shot ayon sa kabuuang $M_J$ ay nagtatapon sa dalawang\n"
"halves, at ang pagpapataw ng $M_J$ sa mga muling pinagsamang product ay pinapanatili ang mga ito. Ipinapaliwanag ng parehong argumento kung bakit\n"
"hindi kailangan ng `recover_configurations` ang anumang kaalaman sa $M_J$ para maging kapaki-pakinabang sa kasong ito.\n"

